&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Remote within Europe, with regular presence in Bremen&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct Reports:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;None&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working Model: &lt;/strong&gt;Remote / hybrid. Regular time on-site in Bremen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Mission&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Own build, deployment and infrastructure for scientific software that runs in awkward places — customer premises, restricted laboratory networks, air-gapped sites, and our own cloud. The role combines conventional cloud platform engineering with the harder problem of shipping updatable software into environments we do not control.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 1 Deployment and Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own build, CI/CD and release for the platform across cloud and on-premise targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain installers and update paths that work in restricted and offline environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage database migration and rollback paths for customer installations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Success Metrics and KPIs: release frequency, failed deployments, time to patch a customer site.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 2 Infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the Kubernetes and GitOps side of the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own secrets management, access control and infrastructure-as-code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement monitoring and log aggregation across internal and customer environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate with Constructor&#39;s platform, identity and deployment tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Success Metrics and KPIs: uptime, mean time to detect, infrastructure reproducible from code.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar 3 Security and Governance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introduce static analysis and dependency and licence scanning into the pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own backup, recovery and continuity for the platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support audit and compliance requirements from funded research and customer contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Accountability: no single undocumented dependency on one person, including yourself.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Requirements&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong AWS or equivalent, Kubernetes, and configuration management such as Ansible, at production scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real experience of on-premise and offline deployment, not only cloud.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CI/CD pipeline ownership end to end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Competencies&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomous and proactive. You have carried infrastructure alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to hand knowledge over rather than hold it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interested in the product and the science, not only the pipeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communicator in English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education &amp;amp; Languages&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in computer science or engineering, or equivalent practical track record.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What This Role Is (and Is Not)&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role IS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full ownership of infrastructure for a technically unusual product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A role where you finally get a team around you.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to a broad modern stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This role is NOT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A pure cloud or pure on-premise role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A ticket-driven operations role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A role without contact with the

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Welcome to Planet. We believe in using space to help life on Earth.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Planet designs, builds, and operates the largest constellation of imaging satellites in history. This constellation delivers an unprecedented dataset of empirical information via a revolutionary cloud-based platform to authoritative figures in commercial, environmental, and humanitarian sectors. We are both a space company and data company all rolled into one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Customers and users across the globe use Planet&#39;s data to develop new technologies, drive revenue, power research, and solve our world’s toughest obstacles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we control every component of hardware design, manufacturing, data processing, and software engineering, our office is a truly inspiring mix of experts from a variety of domains.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have a people-centric approach toward culture and community and we strive to iterate in a way that puts our team members first and prepares our company for growth. Join Planet and be a part of our mission to change the way people see the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Planet is a global company with employees working remotely world wide and joining us from offices in San Francisco, Washington DC, Germany, Austria, Slovenia, and The Netherlands.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Reliability Engineer with focus on Identity and Access Management (IAM) to join the Corporate Engineering team. As an SRE together with other engineers you will be responsible for the continuous operation, further development and enhancement of Planet’s corporate infrastructure and applications, acting as the technical authority for our enterprise identity ecosystem.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time, hybrid role which will require you to work from our Berlin, Haarlem or Ljubljana office 3 days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Impact You’ll Own:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help to ensure the operation of Planet’s internal IT systems, specifically architecting and maintaining our identity providers (Okta, Auth0, Keycloak).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve existing and create new solutions by engineering automated zero-day Joiner, Mover, and Leaver (JML) workflows directly from our HRIS (e.g., HiBob).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scripting &amp;amp; Tooling: Use Python or Go to automate repetitive tasks, build custom provisioning connectors for legacy applications, and enforce identity data minimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and reduce operational toil through automation, making our systems self-healing and predictable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Infrastructure as Code (IaC): Leverage APIs, Terraform, Ansible, or SaltStack to manage configurations as code, moving away from manual UI/CLI changes across our identity platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in an on-call rotation and drive the continuous improvement of incident response, root cause analysis (RCA), and post-mortem processes for complex authentication failures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Security and other IT teams to embed reliability, scalability, and security best practices from the ground up, ensuring our identity architecture complies with GDPR and Zero Trust principles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years experience in infrastructure development and/or operations, with a dedicated focus on Identity and Access Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;2,1,0&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree in a related field or equivalent professional experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-path-to-node=&quot;2,1,0&quot;&gt;Expertise with a scripting language like Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of working with large web applications or comput

&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Data Platform Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join the &lt;strong&gt;Data Platform&lt;/strong&gt; at Smartly!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Smartly is building the standard path for governed data sharing across product services, analytics, and AI/ML. The Data Platform team owns the contracts, control mechanisms, publication paths, catalog metadata, lifecycle rules, lineage, permissions, and runtime building blocks that make reusable data safe and practical at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a role for someone who wants to shape a platform early, while working on concrete production problems from the start. Smartly already has the production systems, Kafka backbone, PostgreSQL databases, analytical consumers, and AI/ML use cases that need a better data foundation. The challenge is to turn that reality into a standard path that engineers actually want to use.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our first milestone is focused: centrally managed publishing tables in service-owned PostgreSQL databases, captured through Debezium CDC into Kafka, and registered in DataHub with ownership, lifecycle, lineage, and impact-analysis metadata. Longer-term, the platform expands toward self-service data products, governed materialisations, durable shared state, and reusable data across Smartly’s operational and analytical systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is not a role where you only maintain an existing reporting pipeline. You will help design and build the platform path that other engineering teams use when they publish and consume shared data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What you will do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build platform services, tools, and workflows for contract-driven data publishing and consumption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the first production path for platform-managed PostgreSQL publishing tables, Debezium CDC, Kafka topics, and catalog registration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create GitOps-style workflows where contracts, schemas, ownership, lifecycle, compatibility, policy metadata, and runtime desired state are reviewed, validated, and reconciled as code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build tooling that gives product engineers fast feedback before they publish or change data products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define how Smartly models data products, publishing contracts, schema evolution, field stability, deletion semantics, access policy, lineage, and cost attribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate and improve the CDC runtime model, including Kubernetes workloads, source-specific isolation, offsets, schema history, heartbeats, signal channels, lag visibility, replay, resnapshotting, and recovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate platform metadata into DataHub so engineers can discover data products, understand ownership, trace lineage, and reason about the impact of changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with product, infrastructure, data engineering, analytics, and AI/ML teams to make the standard path easier and safer than bespoke point-to-point integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What we are looking for&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience building and operating production software systems, preferably in platform, infrastructure, backend, or data-intensive environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of distributed systems trade-offs: reliability, idempotency, replay, eventual consistency, ownership boundaries, compatibility, and operational failure modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience with PostgreSQL or other relational databases, including schema design, migrations, transactions, replication, or operational performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Kafka, event streaming, CDC, Debezium, or adjacent data-movement technologies. Direct Debezium experience is valuable, but strong fundamentals matter more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building software that other engineers use: CLIs, internal platforms, control planes, automation, CI validation, devel

